[TITLE]
NUM-48: STEADY routing, a constant 1 cfs inflow at 10 mg/L of P1 enters J1
and flows through conduit C1 to outfall O1. P1 has K1 = -24/day, which the
input reader accepts as growth. Routing step 300 s.
Over one step eq. 5-6 gives 10*exp(+24/86400*300) = 10.869 mg/L in C1;
any growth at all puts C1 above the 10 mg/L it receives.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         STEADY
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    01/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             02:00:00
DRY_STEP             00:05:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
ROUTING_STEP         300
REPORT_STEP          00:30:00

[JUNCTIONS]
J1   2   5   0   0   0

[OUTFALLS]
O1   0   FREE

[CONDUITS]
C1  J1  O1  400  0.013  0  0  0

[XSECTIONS]
C1  CIRCULAR  2  0  0  0  1

[POLLUTANTS]
;;Name Units Crain Cgw Crdii Kdecay SnowOnly CoPollut CoFrac Cdwf Cinit
P1  MG/L  0  0  0  -24  NO  *  0  0  0

[INFLOWS]
;;Node Param TimeSeries Type Mfactor Sfactor Baseline
J1  FLOW  ""  FLOW  1.0  1.0  1
J1  P1    ""  CONCEN  1.0  1.0  10

[REPORT]
NODES ALL
LINKS ALL
